        <h2 id="order">Hook order</h2>

        <p>
            Hooks are sourced once while building and again by
            <code>/init</code> at boot. <code>build_hook</code> populates the
            archive. <code>run_early_hook</code> runs before root mount.
            <code>run_late_hook</code> runs after root mount.
            <code>run_cleanup_hook</code> runs during teardown, in reverse hook order.
        </p>

        <pre><code>mkinitramfs -s encrypt -a udev -m dm_mod -b cryptsetup -o /boot/initrd-custom.img</code></pre>
        <h2 id="examples">Examples</h2>

        <pre><code>mkinitramfs
mkinitramfs -k "$(uname -r)" -o /boot/initrd-linux.img
mkinitramfs -C zstd -A automod -s udev
mkinitramfs -m ext4,ahci,nvme -b /bin/bash -f /etc/crypttab</code></pre>

        <p>
            Run as root. Confirm the output path is on the boot filesystem and
            inspect it with
            <a href="#/mkinitramfs/lsmkinitramfs">lsmkinitramfs</a> before
            rebooting.
        </p>
    </article>
